## Primary Data Flow: Recipe Input → PDF Output

**PDF rendering is 100% client-side now.** Backend never sees the recipe.

1. User searches → `GET /api/search?query=` → ranked list (top 40)
2. Selects food → `GET /api/food/{fdc_id}` → `MacroProfile` (per 100g) + `PortionSize[]`
3. `recipeStore.addIngredient(Omit<IngredientItem,"instanceId">)` — assigns UUID `instanceId`
   - `baseMacros` cached per row (raw per-100g, never scaled)
   - `availablePortions` cached so unit picker still works after food detail query is gone
4. `useNutritionCalc()` → `calculateRecipeMacros(ingredients, portionDivisor)` → **unrounded** per-serving `MacroProfile`
5. `<LabelPreview>` (DOM) and `<LabelPdfDoc>` (@react-pdf/renderer) both read GEO + row metadata from `components/label/labelSpec.ts` and call `rowDisplay()` — the SAME resolver — so preview and downloadable PDF cannot drift on values, rounding, or %DV.
6. "Save PDF" → `@react-pdf/renderer.pdf(<LabelPdfDoc/>).toBlob()` in-browser → `downloadBlob()`.

**No backend round-trip for label generation.** The retired POST `/api/generate_label` (WeasyPrint) is gone; see the comment at the end of `backend/app/main.py`.

