## Constants (must stay in sync: backend ↔ frontend)

### UNIT_CONVERSIONS → grams  (`constants.py` / `utils/units.ts`)
```
g: 1.0 | ml: 1.0 (water-density assumption) | oz: 28.3495 | lb: 453.592 | kg: 1000.0
```

### FDA_DAILY_VALUES 2020  (`constants.py` / `utils/nutrition.ts`)
```
fat_total_g: 78       fat_saturated_g: 20    cholesterol_mg: 300    sodium_mg: 2300
carbohydrates_total_g: 275    fiber_g: 28    vitamin_d_mcg: 20      calcium_mg: 1300
iron_mg: 18           potassium_mg: 4700
```
`calories`, `sugar_g`, `protein_g` → **no %DV** (render em-dash). Added Sugars DV = 50g (frontend-only, `ADDED_SUGARS_DV`).

### NUTRIENT_FIELDS — 13 keys, FDA label order
```
calories, fat_total_g, fat_saturated_g, cholesterol_mg, sodium_mg,
carbohydrates_total_g, fiber_g, sugar_g, protein_g,
vitamin_d_mcg, calcium_mg, iron_mg, potassium_mg
```

### FDA rounding increments (frontend `formatNutrientAmount`, 21 CFR 101.9(c))
```
calories:                <5 → "0"; ≤50 → nearest 5; else nearest 10
fat_total_g / fat_sat:   <0.5 → "0g"; <5 → nearest 0.5g; else nearest 1g
trans_fat:               same as fat (formatTransFatAmount)
cholesterol_mg:          <2 → "0mg"; ≤5 → "less than 5mg"; else nearest 5
sodium_mg:               <5 → "0mg"; ≤140 → nearest 5; else nearest 10
carbs / fiber / sugar / protein / added_sugars:
                         <0.5 → "0g"; <1 → "less than 1g"; else nearest 1g
vitamin_d_mcg / iron_mg: nearest 0.1
calcium_mg / potassium_mg: nearest 10
%DV (macros):            nearest 1
%DV (micros):            ≤10 → nearest 2; ≤50 → nearest 5; else nearest 10; "<1%" when >0 rounds to 0
```

### Validation limits (backend `models.py`)
```
name length: 120 chars         ingredient amount: >0 ≤ 1,000,000
max_body_bytes: 64 KB
```
(`ingredients: 1–100`, `portion_divisor: 1–999`, `width_inches: 2–12`, `height_inches: 2–20` all still declared on `GenerateLabelRequest` for tests — unused at runtime.)

### Label defaults (frontend)
```
